{"event": "LIFE_CYCLE_COMPLETED", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T04:42:11.716745+00:00", "cycle": 5, "goal_id": "integration", "padge_response": "{\"goal\": \"Add deterministic Ed25519 signature verification for federation proposals and expose it via the public omega API\", \"reason\": \"Existing federation modules validate proposal structure but lack cryptographic signature verification, which is essential for trust and security when ingesting proposals from external participants.\", \"changes\": [{\"path\": \"omega/federation_proposal_signature.py\", \"content\": \"'''\\\\\\nUtilities for verifying Ed25519 signatures on federation proposals.\\n\\\\\\nA federation proposal is expected to be a mapping with at least the following\\nkeys:\\n\\n* ``payload`` – the canonical JSON‑serialisable object that was signed.\\n* ``signature`` – the Ed25519 signature of the UTF‑8 encoded payload,\\n  encoded as a lower‑case hex string.\\n\\\\\\nThe function :func:`verify_federation_proposal_signature` returns ``True`` if\\nthe signature is valid for the supplied public key, otherwise ``False``.\\n'''\\\\\\n\\\\\\nimport json\\nimport binascii\\nfrom typing import Mapping, Any\\n\\\\\\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PublicKey\\nfrom cryptography.exceptions import InvalidSignature\\n\\\\\\n\\\\\\ndef _canonical_payload(payload: Any) -> bytes:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\\\n    Produce a deterministic byte representation of ``payload`` using\\n    ``json.dumps`` with ``sort_keys=True`` and UTF‑8 encoding.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return json.dumps(\\n        payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")\\n    ).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\\\\\n\\\\\\ndef verify_federation_proposal_signature(\\n    proposal: Mapping[str, Any], public_key_hex: str\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\\\n    Verify the Ed25519 signature embedded in a federation proposal.\\n\\\\\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    proposal:\\n        The full proposal dictionary. It must contain ``payload`` and\\n        ``signature`` fields.\\n    public_key_hex:\\n        The public key of the signer as a lower‑case hex string (64\\n        hexadecimal characters).\\n\\\\\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    bool\\n        ``True`` if the signature is correct, ``False`` otherwise.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        signature_hex = proposal[\\\"signature\\\"]\\n        payload = proposal[\\\"payload\\\"]\\n    except KeyError:\\n        return False\\n\\\\\\n    try:\\n        signature = binascii.unhexlify(signature_hex)\\n        public_key_bytes = binascii.unhexlify(public_key_hex)\\n    except (binascii.Error, ValueError):\\n        return False\\n\\\\\\n    message = _canonical_payload(payload)\\n\\\\\\n    try:\\n        pub_key = Ed25519PublicKey.from_public_bytes(public_key_bytes)\\n        pub_key.verify(signature, message)\\n        return True\\n    except (InvalidSignature, ValueError):\\n        return False\\n\"}, {\"path\": \"omega/__init__.py\", \"content\": \"(# Existing content of omega/__init__.py is preserved and the following lines are appended)\\\\\\n\\\\\\n# Federation proposal signature verification\\\\\\ntry:\\\\\\n    from .federation_proposal_signature import verify_federation_proposal_signature\\\\\\n    if \\\"__all__\\\" in globals():\\\\\\n        __all__.append(\\\"verify_federation_proposal_signature\\\")\\\\\\n    else:\\\\\\n        __all__ = [\\\"verify_federation_proposal_signature\\\"]\\\\\\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover\\\\\\n    # If the import fails we keep the package importable; the function will be\\\\\\n    # unavailable until the module is correctly placed.\\n    pass\"}]}", "execution": "PADGE_RESPONSE_RECEIVED", "code_integration": "NOT_ASSERTED"}
