{"event": "LIFE_CYCLE_COMPLETED", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T05:14:34.661469+00:00", "cycle": 7, "goal_id": "federation", "padge_response": "{\"goal\": \"Agregar verificación de conectividad para participantes federados, permitiendo validar de forma determinista que los endpoints declarados son alcanzables antes de su asimilación.\", \"reason\": \"El subsistema de federación carece de una herramienta para comprobar la disponibilidad de los servicios de los participantes (p.ej., endpoints HTTPS). Esta capacidad es esencial para las fases de descubrimiento, validación y estado, y permite detectar problemas de red, DNS o recursos antes de intentar la asimilación de propuestas.\", \"changes\": [{\"path\": \"omega/federation_connectivity.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"omega.federation_connectivity\\n=================================\\nUtilities for deterministic connectivity checks of federated participants.\\n\\nThe federation subsystem already provides registration, proposal handling and\\nassimilation, but it does not verify that the network endpoints advertised by\\nparticipants are actually reachable.  This module offers a lightweight, pure\\nstandard‑library implementation that:\\n\\n* Parses ``http`` and ``https`` URLs.\\n* Resolves hostnames to IP addresses (IPv4/IPv6) with a short timeout.\\n* Attempts a TCP connection to the target port.\\n* Optionally upgrades to TLS for ``https`` endpoints.\\n* Returns a boolean flag together with a human‑readable diagnostic message.\\n* Caches recent results for a configurable TTL to avoid unnecessary network\\n  traffic during bulk operations.\\n\\nThe API is deliberately simple so it can be used from higher‑level orchestration\\ncode (e.g. ``omega.federation_candidate_orchestrator``) without introducing new\\nruntime dependencies.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport socket\\nimport ssl\\nimport time\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\\nfrom typing import Any, Mapping, Tuple\\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Simple in‑memory cache for recent connectivity results.\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass _CacheEntry:\\n    reachable: bool\\n    message: str\\n    expires_at: float\\n\\n# Cache keyed by ``(scheme, host, port)``\\n_CONNECTIVITY_CACHE: dict[Tuple[str, str, int], _CacheEntry] = {}\\n# Default TTL for cached entries (seconds)\\n_DEFAULT_TTL = 60.0\\n\\ndef _cache_key(scheme: str, host: str, port: int) -> Tuple[str, str, int]:\\n    return (scheme.lower(), host.lower(), port)\\n\\ndef _store_in_cache(scheme: str, host: str, port: int, reachable: bool, message: str, ttl: float) -> None:\\n    expires = time.time() + ttl\\n    _CONNECTIVITY_CACHE[_cache_key(scheme, host, port)] = _CacheEntry(reachable, message, expires)\\n\\ndef _lookup_cache(scheme: str, host: str, port: int) -> Tuple[bool, str] | None:\\n    entry = _CONNECTIVITY_CACHE.get(_cache_key(scheme, host, port))\\n    if entry and entry.expires_at > time.time():\\n        return entry.reachable, entry.message\\n    # Stale entry – remove it\\n    if entry:\\n        _CONNECTIVITY_CACHE.pop(_cache_key(scheme, host, port), None)\\n    return None\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Public API\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef check_participant_connectivity(\\n    participant: Mapping[str, Any],\\n    *,\\n    timeout: float = 5.0,\\n    cache_ttl: float = _DEFAULT_TTL,\\n) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Check whether the participant's declared endpoint is reachable.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    participant:\\n        Mapping object that must contain an ``\\\"endpoint\\\"`` key whose value is a\\n        string URL (e.g. ``\\\"https://example.com:8443/api\\\"``).  Additional keys are\\n        ignored.\\n    timeout:\\n        Socket timeout in seconds for DNS resolution and the TCP connect call.\\n    cache_ttl:\\n        Time‑to‑live for cached results.  Use ``0`` to disable caching.\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    (reachable, message):\\n        * ``reachable`` – ``True`` if a TCP (or TLS) connection could be\\n          established, ``False`` otherwise.\\n        * ``message`` – Human‑readable diagnostic describing success or the\\n          failure reason (DNS error, timeout, TLS handshake, etc.).\\n\\n    Notes\\n    -----\\n    The function is deliberately defensive: any exception is caught and turned\\n    into a ``False`` result with an explanatory message.  This guarantees that\\n    callers never have to handle unexpected traceback propagation, simplifying\\n    orchestration logic and testability.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Input validation – fail fast with a clear message.\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    if not isinstance(participant, Mapping):\\n        return False, \\\"participant must be a mapping with an 'endpoint' key\\\"\\n    endpoint = participant.get(\\\"endpoint\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(endpoint, str):\\n        return False, \\\"participant mapping does not contain a valid 'endpoint' string\\\"\\n\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Parse the URL.\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    parsed = urlparse(endpoint)\\n    if parsed.scheme not in {\\\"http\\\", \\\"https\\\"}:\\n        return False, f\\\"unsupported URL scheme '{parsed.scheme}' – only http/https are allowed\\\"\\n    host = parsed.hostname\\n    if not host:\\n        return False, \\\"could not determine hostname from endpoint URL\\\"\\n    port = parsed.port\\n    # Default ports when not explicitly provided.\\n    if port is None:\\n        port = 443 if parsed.scheme == \\\"https\\\" else 80\\n\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Cache lookup.\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    if cache_ttl > 0:\\n        cached = _lookup_cache(parsed.scheme, host, port)\\n        if cached is not None:\\n            return cached\\n\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Resolve DNS – getaddrinfo provides IPv4/IPv6 tuples.\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    try:\\n        addr_info = socket.getaddrinfo(host, port, type=socket.SOCK_STREAM)\\n    except socket.gaierror as exc:\\n        message = f\\\"DNS resolution failed for host '{host}': {exc}\\\"  # noqa: E501\\n        if cache_ttl > 0:\\n            _store_in_cache(parsed.scheme, host, port, False, message, cache_ttl)\\n        return False, message\\n\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Attempt connection to the first resolved address.\\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    success = False\\n    error_msg = \\\"\\\"\\n    for family, socktype, proto, _, sockaddr in addr_info:\\n        try:\\n            with socket.socket(family, socktype, proto) as raw_sock:\\n                raw_sock.settimeout(timeout)\\n                raw_sock.connect(sockaddr)\\n                # For HTTPS we need to wrap the socket with SSL.\\n                if parsed.scheme == \\\"https\\\":\\n                    context = ssl.create_default_context()\\n                    # ``server_hostname`` enables SNI and proper cert verification.\\n                    with context.wrap_socket(raw_sock, server_hostname=host) as ssock:\\n                        ssock.do_handshake()\\n                # If we get here, the connection (and optional TLS) succeeded.\\n                success = True\\n                break\\n        except (socket.timeout, OSError, ssl.SSLError) as exc:\\n            error_msg = str(exc)\\n            # Try the next address (if any).\\n            continue\\n    if success:\\n        message = \\\"reachable\\\"\\n        if cache_ttl > 0:\\n            _store_in_cache(parsed.scheme, host, port, True, message, cache_ttl)\\n        return True, message\\n    else:\\n        message = f\\\"connection failed: {error_msg}\\\" if error_msg else \\\"connection failed\\\"\\n        if cache_ttl > 0:\\n            _store_in_cache(parsed.scheme, host, port, False, message, cache_ttl)\\n        return False, message\\n\\n# Re‑export for ``from omega.federation_connectivity import *``\\n__all__ = [\\\"check_participant_connectivity\\\"]\\n\"}]}", "execution": "PADGE_RESPONSE_RECEIVED", "code_integration": "NOT_ASSERTED"}
