{"event": "LIFE_CYCLE_COMPLETED", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T10:09:43.109896+00:00", "cycle": 14, "goal_id": "resilience", "padge_response": "{\"goal\": \"Add capability to create signed federation proposals offline, enabling deterministic proposal generation for testing and authorized onboarding without external network calls.\", \"reason\": \"Existing federation modules support discovery, validation, and assimilation of proposals but lack a secure, deterministic utility to generate signed proposals from a descriptor and a private Ed25519 key. Implementing this fills the gap, allowing operators and tests to produce valid proposals offline, facilitating end‑to‑end federation workflows while respecting all security constraints.\", \"changes\": [{\"path\": \"omega/federation_proposal_creator.py\", \"content\": \"'''omega.federation_proposal_creator\\n\\nUtility to generate a signed federation proposal from a participant descriptor.\\n\\nThe function operates entirely offline:\\n* It receives a descriptor dictionary describing the participant capabilities.\\n* It receives a raw Ed25519 private key (32‑byte bytes object) supplied by the caller.\\n* It optionally accepts a timestamp; otherwise the current Unix epoch is used.\\n* It returns a deterministic proposal structure containing the payload and a\\n  hex‑encoded Ed25519 signature.\\n\\nThe implementation uses deterministic JSON canonicalisation (sorted keys,\\ncompact separators) to guarantee that identical inputs always produce the same\\nsignature, which is essential for reproducible testing and auditability.\\n\\nThe module does **not** store or expose any secret key material; callers are\\nresponsible for secure key management. The function raises clear exceptions for\\ninvalid inputs, allowing callers to handle errors without side effects.\\n''' \\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport time\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Optional\\n\\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey\\n\\n\\ndef _canonical_json(data: Dict[str, Any]) -> bytes:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a deterministic JSON byte representation of *data*.\\n\\n    The payload is encoded using UTF‑8 with keys sorted and without unnecessary\\n    whitespace. This guarantees that the same logical payload always produces\\n    identical bytes, which is required for deterministic signatures.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef create_signed_proposal(\\n    descriptor: Dict[str, Any],\\n    private_key_bytes: bytes,\\n    *,\\n    timestamp: Optional[int] = None,\\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Create a signed federation proposal.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    descriptor:\\n        A dictionary describing the participant (capabilities, endpoint URLs,\\n        identifiers, etc.). The caller must ensure the descriptor conforms to\\n        the schema expected by the federation validation utilities.\\n    private_key_bytes:\\n        A 32‑byte Ed25519 private key. The function does **not** perform any\\n        key derivation; the raw private key material is required.\\n    timestamp:\\n        Optional Unix epoch seconds. If omitted, the current time is used.\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    dict\\n        A proposal dictionary with two top‑level keys:\\n        * ``payload`` – the deterministic payload containing ``descriptor`` and\\n          ``timestamp``.\\n        * ``signature`` – hex‑encoded Ed25519 signature of the canonical JSON\\n          representation of ``payload``.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not isinstance(descriptor, dict):\\n        raise TypeError(\\\"descriptor must be a dict\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(private_key_bytes, (bytes, bytearray)) or len(private_key_bytes) != 32:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"private_key_bytes must be a 32‑byte Ed25519 private key\\\")\\n\\n    ts = int(timestamp) if timestamp is not None else int(time.time())\\n    payload = {\\\"descriptor\\\": descriptor, \\\"timestamp\\\": ts}\\n    payload_bytes = _canonical_json(payload)\\n\\n    private_key = Ed25519PrivateKey.from_private_bytes(bytes(private_key_bytes))\\n    signature = private_key.sign(payload_bytes)\\n\\n    proposal = {\\n        \\\"payload\\\": payload,\\n        \\\"signature\\\": signature.hex(),\\n    }\\n    return proposal\\n\"}, {\"path\": \"omega/__init__.py\", \"content\": \"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Top‑level package for omega.\\n\\nThis module provides a lazy‑import façade that re‑exports the public API of the\\nfederation subsystem and core utilities. The lazy‑import map is deliberately\\nexplicit to avoid unwanted side‑effects during package import.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport importlib\\nimport sys\\nfrom types import ModuleType\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\n__all__ = [\\n    # Core federation utilities\\n    \\\"federation\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_proposals\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_assimilation\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_processor\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_endpoint_validator\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_network_overview\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_revocation_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_pending_proposals_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_assimilation_controller\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_health\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_participant_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_discovery_control\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_pipeline\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_proposal_creator\\\",\\n]\\n\\n# Mapping from attribute name to the module that implements it.\\n_lazy_imports = {\\n    \\\"federation\\\": \\\"omega.federation\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_proposals\\\": \\\"omega.federation_proposals\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_assimilation\\\": \\\"omega.federation_assimilation\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_processor\\\": \\\"omega.federation_candidate_processor\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_endpoint_validator\\\": \\\"omega.federation_endpoint_validator\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_network_overview\\\": \\\"omega.federation_network_overview\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_revocation_status\\\": \\\"omega.federation_revocation_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_pending_proposals_status\\\": \\\"omega.federation_pending_proposals_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_assimilation_controller\\\": \\\"omega.federation_assimilation_controller\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_health\\\": \\\"omega.federation_health\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_participant_status\\\": \\\"omega.federation_participant_status\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_discovery_control\\\": \\\"omega.federation_candidate_discovery_control\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_candidate_pipeline\\\": \\\"omega.federation_candidate_pipeline\\\",\\n    \\\"federation_proposal_creator\\\": \\\"omega.federation_proposal_creator\\\",\\n}\\n\\ndef __getattr__(name: str) -> Any:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Lazily import sub‑modules when accessed as attributes.\\n\\n    This function is invoked by Python when an attribute lookup on the package\\n    fails. If *name* is present in ``_lazy_imports`` the corresponding module is\\n    imported, cached in ``sys.modules`` and returned. Otherwise ``AttributeError``\\n    is raised.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if name in _lazy_imports:\\n        module_path = _lazy_imports[name]\\n        module = importlib.import_module(module_path)\\n        setattr(sys.modules[__name__], name, module)\\n        return module\\n    raise AttributeError(f\\\"module 'omega' has no attribute {name!r}\\\")\\n\\ndef __dir__() -> list[str]:\\n    return sorted(list(globals().keys()) + list(_lazy_imports.keys()))\\n\"}]}", "execution": "PADGE_RESPONSE_RECEIVED", "code_integration": "NOT_ASSERTED"}
