{"event": "LIFE_CYCLE_COMPLETED", "timestamp": "2026-11-11T03:29:14.411943+00:00", "cycle": 35, "goal_id": "integration", "padge_response": "{\"goal\": \"Agregar módulo de descubrimiento controlado de candidatos federados\", \"reason\": \"La infraestructura carece de una capa que descubra candidatos de forma segura sin registrar automáticamente participantes externos. Este módulo permite leer una lista de candidatos autorizados desde un archivo de control (whitelist) y validar su estructura usando los validadores existentes, facilitando pruebas y orquestación controlada.\", \"changes\": [{\"path\": \"omega/federation_candidate_discovery.py\", \"content\": \"'''omega/federation_candidate_discovery.py\\n\\nMódulo de descubrimiento controlado de candidatos federados.\\n\\nProvee una función `discover_candidates` que lee un archivo de \\\"whitelist\\\"\\n(JSONL) con descripciones de candidatos y devuelve una lista de diccionarios\\nvalidados. No se realiza ningún registro automático ni comunicación de red;\\nsolo se verifica la consistencia estructural utilizando el validador de\\ncandidatos existente si está disponible.\\n\\nEste componente complementa los servicios de gestión, revocación y\\npipeline ya presentes en el paquete `omega` y permite pruebas unitarias\\ncontroladas sin necesidad de contactos externos.\\n'''\\\"\\\"\\\"Controlled discovery of federated candidates.\\n\\nThe discovery process is deliberately limited to reading a local whitelist\\nfile supplied by the operator. Each line of the file must be a JSON object\\nrepresenting a candidate with at least the following keys:\\n\\n* ``url`` – HTTPS URL of the candidate node.\\n* ``public_key`` – Ed25519 public key in hex or base64 format.\\n* ``metadata`` – Optional dictionary with additional information.\\n\\nThe function validates each entry using the existing validator (if\\navailable) and returns a list of validated candidate dictionaries.  Invalid\\nentries are collected and reported via a ``ValueError`` containing the\\naggregate error messages.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\\n\\n# Attempt to import the existing validator.  It may not exist in older\\n# revisions; in that case we fall back to a minimal inline validation.\\ntry:\\n    from .federation_candidate_validator import validate_candidate  # type: ignore\\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover\\n    validate_candidate = None  # noqa: N806\\n\\n\\ndef _minimal_validate(candidate: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Perform a minimal structural validation of a candidate.\\n\\n    This is a safety net used when the dedicated validator module is not\\n    present.  It checks that required fields exist and have plausible types.\\n    The function raises ``ValueError`` if the candidate is malformed.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    required_keys = {\\\"url\\\", \\\"public_key\\\"}\\n    missing = required_keys - candidate.keys()\\n    if missing:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required fields: {', '.join(sorted(missing))}\\\")\\n\\n    url = candidate[\\\"url\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(url, str) or not url.startswith(\\\"https://\\\"):\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"'url' must be a HTTPS string, got: {url!r}\\\")\\n\\n    pub_key = candidate[\\\"public_key\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(pub_key, str) or len(pub_key) < 30:\\n        # No strict length check – just ensure it looks like a key string.\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"'public_key' must be a non‑empty string, got: {pub_key!r}\\\")\\n\\n    # ``metadata`` is optional; if present it must be a dict.\\n    if \\\"metadata\\\" in candidate and not isinstance(candidate[\\\"metadata\\\"], dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'metadata' must be a dictionary if provided\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef discover_candidates(whitelist_path: str | Path) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Discover and validate candidates from a whitelist file.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    whitelist_path: str or pathlib.Path\\n        Path to a file where each line is a JSON object describing a candidate.\\n        Blank lines and lines starting with ``#`` are ignored, allowing simple\\n        comments.\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    List[Dict[str, Any]]\\n        A list of validated candidate dictionaries ready to be passed to the\\n        higher‑level candidate pipeline or manager.\\n\\n    Raises\\n    ------\\n    FileNotFoundError\\n        If the supplied path does not exist.\\n    ValueError\\n        If any candidate entry fails validation.  All errors are aggregated and\\n        reported together to aid debugging.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    path = Path(whitelist_path)\\n    if not path.is_file():\\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\\\"Whitelist file not found: {path}\\\")\\n\\n    valid_candidates: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\\n    errors: List[str] = []\\n\\n    with path.open(\\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fp:\\n        for line_no, raw in enumerate(fp, start=1):\\n            line = raw.strip()\\n            if not line or line.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\\n                continue  # skip comments / empty lines\\n            try:\\n                candidate = json.loads(line)\\n                if not isinstance(candidate, dict):\\n                    raise ValueError(\\\"Candidate entry must be a JSON object\\\")\\n            except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\\n                errors.append(f\\\"Line {line_no}: invalid JSON – {exc.msg}\\\")\\n                continue\\n            # Validation: prefer the central validator if available.\\n            try:\\n                if validate_candidate is not None:\\n                    # The validator is expected to raise ``ValueError`` on failure.\\n                    validate_candidate(candidate)  # type: ignore[arg-type]\\n                else:  # pragma: no cover\\n                    _minimal_validate(candidate)\\n                valid_candidates.append(candidate)\\n            except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\\n                errors.append(f\\\"Line {line_no}: {exc}\\\")\\n\\n    if errors:\\n        # Aggregate errors to provide a clear report.\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Candidate discovery failed with the following errors:\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(errors))\\n\\n    return valid_candidates\\n\"}]}", "execution": "PADGE_RESPONSE_RECEIVED", "code_integration": "NOT_ASSERTED"}
